# Build products. Everything here is regenerated by ./build.sh, and the whole
# point of the toolchain is that it can be: design.py is the source of truth.
build/

# The fabrication outputs under fab/ are deliberately NOT ignored -- they are
# the deliverable, and having them in the tree is what lets a change to the
# board be reviewed as a diff.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# KiCad writes this alongside the project to remember window layout, the
# selected layer and similar per-user state. It is not part of the design.
rmc-pizz-arco/*.kicad_prl

# JetBrains project settings. Per-user editor state, not part of the design.
.idea/

.DS_Store
*.iml

# TI's OPA191 macromodel, fetched for the simulation schematic. Their licence
# grants use, not redistribution, and this repository is public -- so the file
# is fetched locally and never committed. gen_sim.py says where to get it and
# generates the sheet whether or not it is present.
#
# There is no equivalent line for the CD4066B because TI publish no SPICE model
# for it at all; gen_sim.py models the switch instead. See its MODEL_FILE
# comment.
rmc-pizz-arco/*.LIB

# The unzipped staging copy of the gerbers. build.sh deletes and rebuilds it
# every run, and rmc-pizz-arco-pcbway.zip beside it holds byte-identical
# content -- so tracking both means ~1100 lines of churn per build for a
# second copy of the same thing. The zip is the deliverable; this is scratch.
fab/pcbway/